# Ismark Kolyanovich travelling with the party (docs/voice/ismark.md): short lines a guest says while walking with the party, shown and voiced
# like banter (story/banter.gd). The node's name says when it may play: quest_ on entering an area while their story is
# at that point (these come first), place_ on entering an area, fight_ after a won fight, idle_ now and then on the
# road. Each plays once per playthrough, only while Ismark is with the party. Every line here is unvoiced for now.

~ place_blood_of_the_vine
if guest:ismark and at:blood_of_the_vine
interject guest:ismark: My corner table. They keep it for me now. It's the nearest thing to a title I've got.
endif
-> END

~ place_village
if guest:ismark and region:village_of_barovia
interject guest:ismark: Welcome back to Barovia. The wine's still sour and the bread's still grey. Nobody's improved anything while we were away.
endif
-> END

~ place_vallaki
if guest:ismark and region:vallaki
interject guest:ismark: Vallaki. Walls, and a baron who thinks a festival can keep out the dark. Well. It beats wolves at the window.
endif
-> END

~ place_krezk
if guest:ismark and region:krezk
interject guest:ismark: Krezk shuts its gate on everyone. I respect that. I'd have done the same, if our gate had ever held.
endif
-> END

~ place_castle
if guest:ismark and region:castle_ravenloft
interject guest:ismark: The landlord's house. Father came up these steps once, to beg. He came back down and never spoke of it.
endif
-> END

~ fight_speech
if guest:ismark
interject guest:ismark: Still alive. Father would have made a speech. I'll just have a drink, if anyone's carrying one.
endif
-> END

~ fight_lesser
if guest:ismark
interject guest:ismark: Ismark the Lesser, still standing. Somebody tell the village. They'll want to be disappointed.
endif
-> END

~ fight_fingers
if guest:ismark
interject guest:ismark: Count your fingers. I always count mine. One day the number will be wrong, and I'll want to know when.
endif
-> END

~ idle_useful
if guest:ismark
interject guest:ismark: I'd die for her. I'd prefer to do something more useful first, but the offer stands.
endif
-> END

~ idle_disasters
if guest:ismark
interject guest:ismark: Every disaster I can think of, I've already imagined. It leaves the real ones very little room to surprise me.
endif
-> END

~ idle_sister
if guest:ismark and guest:ireena
interject guest:ismark: Keep her in the middle of us. She'll hate it. Do it anyway, and blame me.
endif
-> END
